/// \class GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower
/// \ingroup grp_w1020_special_power_module_factories
/// \brief Special-ability update module registered as
///        "GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower", configured by a command
///        button, an upgrade name and toggle flags.
///
/// Registered with the update interface, not the special-power one (see
/// the group page). It overrides the same special-ability trigger function
/// as LevelGrantSpecialPower::triggerAbilityEffect, and it carries
/// per-object state of its own: its constructor clears two fields after
/// the base constructor runs. Neither Zero Hour nor Open-BFME-1 has the
/// class, so its behaviour can only be read from the BFME 2 bodies.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPowerModuleData, after the
/// shared special-ability fields: \c CommandButton and \c UpgradeToGive
/// (names, stored as text) and \c FlagsUsedForToggle (read by a dedicated
/// parser; by its name, a set of flags).
/// \see GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPowerModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1020_special_power_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower: the shared
///        special-ability fields plus command button, upgrade and toggle
///        flags.
///
/// Built by GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData;
/// the field list is on GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower.

/// \fn Module *GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
