/// (chained on the special-ability table) as the field source.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see GiveOrRestoreUpgradeSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class GrabPassengerSpecialPower
/// \ingroup grp_w1020_special_power_module_factories
/// \brief Special power module registered as "GrabPassengerSpecialPower":
///        a power used on a target object, or untargeted, with a grab
///        radius and a tree option.
///
/// A SpecialPowerModule subclass with no per-object state of its own
/// (see the group page). It replaces two of the three entry points and
/// keeps SpecialPowerModule::doSpecialPowerAtLocation:
/// - GrabPassengerSpecialPower::doSpecialPowerAtObject handles a target
///   object.
/// - The untargeted entry point picks a target itself: the closest
///   suitable object within \c GrabRadius of its own object. With
///   \c AllowTree set, and only for one of the command options, a point
///   supplied by the terrain logic can be chosen instead. The chosen
///   object or point is then handed to the owner's special-power module
///   for one particular special-power type (looked up by type on the
///   owning object), through that module's object or location entry
///   point. Which module receives it depends on the object's modules and
///   the SpecialPower definitions they use; it can be this module itself,
///   since GrabPassengerSpecialPower::doSpecialPowerAtObject checks whether
///   its own power has that same type.
///
/// The shared
/// special-ability table has related fields
/// (\c GrabPassengerAnimAndDuration, \c GrabPassengerHealGainPercent),
/// which suggests the power works together with a special-ability update
/// module on the same object; that pairing is not verified here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields of GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData, after the shared
/// special-power fields: \c GrabRadius (real) and \c AllowTree (bool).
/// \see GrabPassengerSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1020_special_power_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for GrabPassengerSpecialPower: the shared
///        special-power fields plus a radius and a tree flag.
///
/// Built by GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData; the
/// field list is on GrabPassengerSpecialPower.

/// \fn Module *GrabPassengerSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "GrabPassengerSpecialPower":
///        creates the module for one object.
///
/// Same pattern as CloudBreakSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built.
/// \param moduleData  The template's shared
///                    GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData.
/// \return The new module, as a Module pointer.
/// \see GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "GrabPassengerSpecialPower": creates
///        the module data and parses the INI block into it.
///
/// Same pattern as CloudBreakSpecialPowerModuleData::friend_newModuleData,
/// with GrabPassengerSpecialPowerModuleData::buildFieldParse as the field
/// source.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null.
/// \return The new module data, as a ModuleData pointer.
/// \see GrabPassengerSpecialPower::friend_newModuleInstance


